# Claude Code local state (machine-specific permissions, absolute paths)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent worktrees. They belong HERE rather than in a session scratchpad under
# /tmp: /tmp is tmpfs, so a reboot empties it and leaves a live registration in
# .git/worktrees pointing at nothing. That orphan broke every tp-backup daily
# run for eight days (2026-08-28..09-03) -- see bin/.local/bin/tp-backup.
.claude/worktrees/

# htop writes htoprc via mkstemp+rename inside the folded package dir; a killed
# htop can leave the temp file behind
htop/.config/htop/htoprc.tmp.*

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

__pycache__/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered palette files.
#
# `theme` renders every *.tmpl against palettes.toml. The output is a build
# artefact: editing one is pointless, since the next switch overwrites it.
#
# This used to be twenty-two paths listed one by one, because a pointer had to
# take the exact filename an application's include names and no glob could
# catch that set without also catching tracked files. Generation chooses the
# output name, so a glob can.
*.gen
*.gen.*

# ...but not the templates they are rendered from, whose names necessarily
# contain the same marker: colors.gen.css.tmpl renders to colors.gen.css.
!*.tmpl

# The exception, and the reason it is an exception: these are read at a fixed
# path by an application that takes no include directive, so their rendered
# output has nowhere to put the .gen marker. The list is structural rather than
# growing — it can only change if an application with a hardcoded config
# filename joins the desktop.
#
# It has changed exactly once since it was written: six paths for GTK and
# xsettingsd, then a seventh when yazi arrived on 2026-08-16. Two applications,
# same cause. A third would be unremarkable; a third *without* that cause would
# mean someone has stopped naming rendered files `*.gen.*`, which is what makes
# the glob above possible.
gtk/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
gtk/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini
gtk/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css
gtk/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini
gtk/.config/xsettingsd/xsettingsd.conf
gtk/.gtkrc-2.0
yazi/.config/yazi/theme.toml

# The active palette used to be recorded here as `.theme`. It now lives in
# $XDG_STATE_HOME/theme/palette (default ~/.local/state), because which palette
# is applied is state belonging to this machine, not to the configuration, and
# state does not belong in a source tree. `theme` migrates the old file once.


# .ruff_cache/ sits at the repo root — a stray from CodeRabbit's ruff runs.
# It's harmless and self-managing (ruff writes its own .gitignore containing *,
# which is why the tree still reads clean), so nothing is at risk of being committed.
# But it's clutter in a tree that's otherwise tidy, and the repo doesn't use ruff itself.
.ruff_cache/

